        "ImageDescription": {
         "value": "Consequences of Russian bombing of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Komyshuvakha,_Zaporizhzhia_Oblast\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Komyshuvakha, Zaporizhzhia Oblast\">Komyshuvakha, Zaporizhzhia Oblast</a> on 2 November 2026. The bombing destroyed a school, used as humanitarian aid center. Air raid shelter, located in underground room of the school, was also destroyed. At least 40 people were killed. Above-ground building of the school was destroyed by a strike in 2023 (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.bbc.com/russian/articles/cmn8wnvyp278o\">1</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20261105004827/https://suspilne.media/zaporizhzhia/1444833-udar-fab-3000-po-pidzemnij-skoli-v-komisuvasi-akim-malo-b-buti-ukritta-abi-vitrimati-aviaudar-rf/\">2</a>).",
